WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Yemen's government has launched a major offensive against Houthi held territory, testing whether outside powers can contain the fighting spread into key shipping lanes. This is Omni View, episode 196. Yemen's internationally recognized government announced a new military campaign aimed at retaking areas held by Houthi forces. The move follows Houthi actions that cut a main road between the cities of Taiz and Aden. Government forces describe the operation as a bad

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.140
battle for liberation. The announcement came on Sunday and targets territory the Houthis

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.480
have held for years. Deutschewella reports the offensive as a direct response to recent

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:46.400
Houthi moves that disrupted internal supply lines inside Yemen. Al-Jazeera frames the

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.940
same announcement as an escalation that could draw in additional regional actors already

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.400
active in the conflict. Both outlets note the operation targets territory the Houthis

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.700
have controlled for years.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.000
Dewey Chavella adds that the government acted after rebels severed a key transport link.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.480
Al Jazeera emphasizes the declaration of a full battle for liberation.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.060
The two accounts converge on the fact of the road closure, but diverge on how much the

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.340
step signals broader regional involvement.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.760
Observers will watch whether government forces achieve measurable territorial gains in the

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.260
coming weeks, or whether the fighting triggers new restrictions on Red Sea shipping.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.540
The Euro reached its weakest level against the US dollar since May 2025.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.620
Markets reacted to political developments in Spain and France that raised questions

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.640
about fiscal plans in both countries.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:45.220
The Eurozone currency was last 0.6% lower against the greenback, according to LSEG data.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.980
Spain is expected to head for a snap election, while France faces scrutiny over its budget

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.500
trajectory.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.060
CNBC highlights investor concern that political volatility in two large euro-area economies

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.020
could keep borrowing costs elevated even as inflation pressures ease elsewhere.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.600
The Guardian notes Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez's planned press conference follows

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.920
Parliamentary rejection of housing measures, with speculation that an early election could follow.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.760
Barkley's economists, cited by CNBC, state that France's draft budget is unlikely to meet

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.940
its deficit targets even if passed.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.280
CNBC adds that the Euro-area faces low growth and a fragmented bond market on top of the

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.360
political uncertainty.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.020
The Guardian records that Sanchez had previously said he would complete a full four-year term

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.660
before the defeat's prompted fresh questions.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:44.720
Federal authorities arrested one Ying Zheng at Los Angeles International Airport and accused

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.060
her of acting as a Chinese foreign agent.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:52.600
President. Prosecutors alleged she collected photos and videos of Taiwan President Lai Chingte's

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:58.660
son and family. US officials say Zhang used trade craft to avoid detection and never

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.700
registered as a foreign agent. The arrest occurred just before Zhang was scheduled to depart

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:09.020
for China. Al Jazeera notes the case involves surveillance of a foreign leader's relative

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:15.200
rather than direct theft of government secrets. The Japan Times emphasizes the failure to notify

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.600
Washington of foreign government work. Al Jazeera and Deutschewella focus on the timing

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:25.480
at the airport and the nature of the alleged surveillance. All three accounts agree on

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.600
the U.S. location and the target of the claimed activity.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:34.380
Pedro Sanchez announced a press conference following Parliament's rejection of two emergency

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.920
housing measures. Protests over rent prices and tenant protections drew tens of thousands

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.560
in Madrid and other cities over the weekend.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:48.380
Sanchez had previously committed to serving a full term, yet the defeats have prompted questions

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:54.040
about his government's ability to pass legislation. Spain's next scheduled election had been set

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:59.720
for next year. Analysts cited in the same coverage note that an early election carries risk,

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:05.680
but could capitalize on current public attention to housing. The Guardian adds that the Parliamentary

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.000
defeats on Friday led to weekend marches in the capital and other cities, with protesters

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.960
demanding action on rents and tenant protections. The same outlet notes that Sanchez is expected

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.340
to address the speculation directly in the coming press conference.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:28.160
BT agreed to buy talk-talk, which has 1.5 million retail customers and 1 million wholesale customers.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.020
The takeover requires approval from the UK's competition and markets authority

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.620
and would end months of uncertainty over Talk Talk's future.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.560
Talk Talk had been on the brink of administration because of its debts.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.760
The deal would give BT greater power over the broadband market.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.940
The BBC reports that BT Chief Executive Alison Kirkby described the deal as a safety net

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:53.660
for households and businesses relying on Talk Talk.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:05:00.400
Competition lawyer Tom Smith told BBC Radio 4 that the regulator will weigh the deal against

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.660
what would happen if Talk Talk exited the market entirely.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:09.100
Some observers have raised concerns about BT's increased share of the broadband market.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.580
The BBC notes that Talk Talk began as a challenger to BT was taken over by private equity

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.460
in 2021 and later built up debt while losing customers.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.720
Kirk be added that the acquisition provides reassurance for employees and for connections

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.040
supporting critical national infrastructure.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:34.180
Recent data show American households maintaining spending levels that have helped sustain overall economic expansion.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.440
The pattern has persisted even as inflation remains above pre-pandemic averages.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.620
Consumer outlays have offset weaker areas such as manufacturing and housing.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:50.460
This resilience has allowed the economy to avoid a sharper slowdown despite higher borrowing costs.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:55.900
The Wall Street Journal reports that consumer outlays have offset weaker areas such as

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.300
manufacturing and housing.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:02.280
The Wall Street Journal adds that the pattern of household spending has continued even

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.600
as prices stay elevated compared with pre-pandemic levels.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:10.500
The same coverage highlights that the strength and consumption has supported broader growth

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.620
figures at a time when other sectors have shown more weakness.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:19.720
Progress worth knowing comes from Hong Kong's new Kai-Tak hospital, which began treating

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.360
patients in its first phase.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.120
Kitech Hospital opened its family medicine center and treated nearly 300 patients on

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:27.900
its first day.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:34.780
Officials project daily visits will reach 1,800 by year end, as more services come online.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:40.760
The hospital is positioned to become Hong Kong's largest public facility, once fully operational.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:46.900
Lawmakers have called for improved connecting transport and clear information on transit options.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:58.680
The South China Morning Post reports that some patients expressed satisfaction with the initial service while lawmakers called for improved connecting transport and clear information on transit options.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:06.780
The South China Morning Post adds that the first phase opening treated nearly 300 patients at the Family Medicine Center on Monday morning.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:14.960
Officials have stated that daily numbers are projected to reach 1,800 by the end of the year as additional services come online.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:15.060
9.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:20.720
To really understand how competition regulators weigh broadband mergers when one firm is

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:25.560
near-collapse, start with the legal test the UK's competition and market's authority

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.300
must apply.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:31.640
The authority compares the proposed merger against the realistic alternative of talk-talk

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:35.820
entering administration and losing its 2.5 million connections.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:41.540
That counterfactual matters because losing an entire provider can reduce choice and raise

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:45.760
prices faster than a merger that keeps the customers on an existing network.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.340
The same logic has appeared in earlier UK cases where failing firms were allowed to combine

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.400
rather than exit.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:58.380
When claims arise that any increase in BT's share is automatically harmful, check whether

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.620
the regulators published reasoning shows the alternative would have been worse for customers.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:09.240
One concrete step is to read the CMA's eventual decision document and note which scenario it

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.280
treats as the baseline.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:15.820
Another useful check is to compare the number of wholesale customers affected against

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:19.760
the number of retail connections that would disappear if talk-talk collapsed.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:25.340
Regulators have previously accepted that preserving service continuity can outweigh concerns

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:29.560
about concentration when the alternative is outright market exit.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:36.000
The CMA will therefore examine both the immediate impact on prices and the longer-term effect

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.960
on infrastructure investment that supports critical national services.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:46.720
CNBC frames the Euros decline through investor concern over fiscal plans in Spain and France,

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:51.740
while the Guardian centers on Sanchez's political position after the housing defeats.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:56.700
Watch whether Spain's government survives the coming weeks without calling an early election.

